  "article_notes": "20 dogs with acute B. gibsoni infection at one private animal hospital in Japan (smear; PCR positive in 18 of 18 tested). The severity measure is pancreatic injury (intercurrent pancreatitis) expressed as the continuous Spec cPL concentration (2 dogs >400 µg/l) and, for one row, serum lipase activity; every row is a Pearson correlation across all 20 dogs. Rows for erythrocyte count, Hb and Ht are what the authors call the 'degree of anaemia' not being related to pancreatitis. CBC, biochemistry and parasitaemia were measured before treatment; serum for cPL was collected after diagnosis. Heart and respiratory rates were often not recorded, so SIRS could not be assessed. Per-dog values are in Table 1; no numbers were computed from it.",
  "skipped_infected_vs_healthy": 0,
